cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The Accuracy Illusion: How overlapping samples manufacture 71% hit-rates
  in intraday index forecasting
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rachit
    family-names: Ranka
    alias: rachitranka25
repository-code: https://github.com/rachitranka25/accuracy-illusion
abstract: >-
  An empirical study of intraday predictability on NSE index derivatives using
  only freely available retail data. Across 100+ strategies and seven model
  families, out-of-sample directional accuracy does not exceed ~50%, and an
  over-capacity model scores identically on real and shuffled labels. Reported
  accuracies of 60-85% are shown to be artefacts of scoring overlapping
  forecasts, which inflates hit-rates 8-11x. Volatility (magnitude) prediction
  reaches 68-74% out-of-sample and is stable, and the variance risk premium is
  identified as the only measurable, retail-reachable positive expectancy.
keywords:
  - market microstructure
  - intraday forecasting
  - negative results
  - overlapping samples
  - volatility forecasting
  - variance risk premium
  - NSE
  - index options
license: MIT
